	<Item Name="Accession" Type="String">GSE180834</Item>
	<Item Name="GDS" Type="String" />
	<Item Name="title" Type="String">Genome-wide CRISPR screen to identfy immune evasion genes in pancreatic cancer</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">Here we systematically dissected PDA intrinsic mechanisms of immune evasion by in vitro and in vivo CRISPR screening. Beyond the conserved set of genes regulating anti-cancer immunity we identified Rnf31 and Vps4b as essential factors required for escaping CD8+ T cell-killing. While the absence of Rnf31 induced sensitivity to T cell killing through TNF-mediated apoptosis in murine cancer cells and human PDA organoids, loss of Vps4b abrogated functional autophagy, resulting in accumulation of CD8+ T cell-derived granzyme B and subsequent tumor cell lysis.</Item>
